      "action_required": true,
      "unaddressed_comments": [
        {
          "id": "pull_comment:4549575663",
          "comment_id": 4549575663,
          "root_comment_id": 4549575663,
          "thread_id": "PRRT_kwDOPmMU8s62lhvt",
          "type": "inline_review_comment",
          "author": "shrutisinghania",
          "path": "core/src/main/java/com/google/cloud/gcs/analyticscore/core/GoogleCloudStorageOutputStream.java",
          "line": 212,
          "diff_hunk": "@@ -195,7 +205,11 @@ public void write(byte[] b, int off, int len) throws IOException {\n   }\n \n   @Override\n-  public void close() throws IOException {\n+  public synchronized void close() throws IOException {\n+    if (closed) {\n+      return;\n+    }\n+    closed = true;",
          "body": "Setting `closed = true` before `channel.close()` means that if `channel.close()` throws (which is where `GcsWriteChannel` awaits `blobWriteSession.getResult().get()` to finalize the upload), any retry of `stream.close()` silently returns without retrying or surfacing an error. Also note that `closed` is `volatile` and `close()` is `synchronized`, while `write(...)` is unsynchronized and the class Javadoc explicitly states this stream is not thread-safe.",
          "created_at": "2026-11-12T11:06:21Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/gcs-analytics-core/pull/490#discussion_r4549575663"
        },
        {
          "id": "pull_comment:4549598008",
          "comment_id": 4549598008,
          "root_comment_id": 4549598008,
          "thread_id": "PRRT_kwDOPmMU8s62llDO",
          "type": "inline_review_comment",
          "author": "shrutisinghania",
          "path": "core/src/test/java/com/google/cloud/gcs/analyticscore/core/GoogleCloudStorageOutputStreamTest.java",
          "line": 508,
          "diff_hunk": "void write_zeroLengthAfterClose_throwsClosedChannelException() throws IOException {\n+    GoogleCloudStorageOutputStream stream =\n+        GoogleCloudStorageOutputStream.create(fakeFileSystem, itemId);\n+    stream.close();\n+\n+    assertThrows(ClosedChannelException.class, () -> stream.write(new byte[0], 0, 0));\n+  }\n+\n+  @Test\n+  void write_afterClose_doesNotRecordWriteMetric() throws IOException {",
          "body": "`mockChannel.write(...)` isn't stubbed, so it returns `0`. If the `checkOpen()` guard ever regresses, `while (buffer.hasRemaining())` spins forever and hangs CI. Please stub `mockChannel.write` to consume the buffer or add `@Timeout`.",
          "created_at": "2026-11-12T11:08:40Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/gcs-analytics-core/pull/490#discussion_r4549598008"
        }
      ],
